Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a1484d21-0dfd-45cd-8284-8c9b01282c59"],

Cell["\<\
S-shaped (sigmoidal) functions rise from 0 to 1 around a threshold. This \
notebook follows them from biology to the mathematics of neural networks. \
Section 0 shows six well-documented biological examples, from the voltage \
gating of ion channels and the oxygen binding of hemoglobin to a genetic \
switch in the fruit-fly embryo, diffusion fronts, logistic population growth \
and the contrast response of visual neurons, and shows that each is the \
logistic function of a scaled and shifted input. Sections 1 and 2 define \
sigmoidal functions and explain why they became the activation of artificial \
neurons. Section 3 states and sketches the proof of Cybenko's universal \
approximation theorem (1989): finite sums of one fixed continuous sigmoid, \
applied to affine functions of the input, approximate every continuous \
function on the unit cube. It also explains, in everyday and in mathematical \
terms, how such a one-hidden-layer network computes and how its gradient \
flows along the arrows of its diagram. Sections 4 and 5 make the theorem \
concrete with staircase constructions in one dimension and least-squares fits \
in two, and relate the rate of convergence to the modulus of continuity. \
Sections 6 and 7 connect the result to Kolmogorov's superposition theorem \
(1957), which answers Hilbert's 13th problem by representing every continuous \
function exactly with one-variable functions and addition. They compare the \
two theorems and the debate over their relevance, and survey later results: \
Hornik, Stinchcombe and White, Hornik, Leshno, Lin, Pinkus and Schocken, \
Barron, and Kolmogorov\[Dash]Arnold networks. Appendix A collects the \
definition, examples and counterexamples of continuity. All formulas are \
checked in Wolfram Language and every figure is reproducible from the \
numbered code cells.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd2515a4-b8c1-4fda-b7d3-69e4cc665a58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Keywords: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "sigmoidal function; logistic function; universal approximation theorem; \
Cybenko; Kolmogorov\[Dash]Arnold superposition theorem; Hilbert's 13th \
problem; neural networks; Hill equation; Boltzmann gating; logistic growth; \
modulus of continuity; Wolfram Language"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ca0c5867-ab9d-4807-a9a8-98551fd07c02"],

