Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0. S functions in living organisms", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c5d6b8c8-538e-4fff-94bc-39df897be855"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Long before artificial neurons, nature was full of S-shaped responses. A \
cell, a protein or a population often reacts weakly to a small stimulus, \
strongly over a narrow middle range, and then saturates. This section \
collects six well-documented examples. Each one, written in the right \
variable, is exactly the logistic function \[Sigma](t) = 1/(1 + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"-", "t"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e6169893-0288-4757-b33a-e0029f2bbd3d"],
 ") of section 2, applied to a scaled and shifted input, \[Sigma](slope \
\[Times] (input - threshold)). That is the same building block as one hidden \
unit \[Sigma](y x + \[Theta]) in Cybenko's network, Eq. (3): the threshold \
plays the role of \[Theta] and the slope the role of y."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f0a6ec4a-226c-49ec-875a-3926282b9aea"],

Cell["\<\
The equations of this section are tagged (0.1)\[Dash](0.6), its figures \
Figure 0.1\[Dash]0.6, its photos Photo 0.1\[Dash]0.6, its references [0.1]\
\[Dash][0.15] and its code cells c.0.1\[Dash]c.0.6 (photo cells \
c.0.1i\[Dash]c.0.6i), so the numbering of the rest of the notebook is \
unchanged. Run c.0 first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"47c69745-5cdf-467a-a242-f17126306ce4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0.1 Voltage gating of ion channels", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f12c1296-2a95-47c1-a990-c5aa06434cad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Voltage-gated ion channels open and close as the membrane voltage changes, \
because charged parts of the protein (the voltage sensor) move in the \
membrane's electric field. Their open probability rises in an S-shape with \
voltage, and it is usually fitted with a two-state Boltzmann function [0.2, \
0.3], characterized by a half-activation voltage ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c4f52674-3efe-4a7a-9a2d-b6ee0dcc8253"],
 " and a slope set by the gating charge z. The same Boltzmann form is \
mathematically analogous to the Hill equation of 0.2."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc35f271-05b2-4b14-b403-b4f550295c37"],

Cell["\<\
Photo 0.1. A squid of the genus Loligo (here the common squid, L. vulgaris). \
Hodgkin and Huxley measured the S-shaped gating of sodium and potassium \
channels on the giant axon of Loligo. Hans Hillewaert, CC BY-SA 4.0, \
Wikimedia Commons.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontSize->14,
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->"e80fcf88-a15f-45ab-87fa-0005ca2318ee"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.0.1i*)
commonsImage[\"Loligo_vulgaris.jpg\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d4f4aee4-c8b1-462c-a914-788dc0d4cb65"],

