Cell["\<\
In a test run the saturation was 0.75 at 40 mmHg and 0.97 at 100 mmHg.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1acab9d1-794d-47b0-b426-c1bf9946ca8f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0.3 A genetic switch: hunchback in the fruit-fly embryo", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"36111641-120c-4c7e-8d02-68baf7554149"],

Cell["\<\
In the early Drosophila embryo the Bicoid protein forms a smooth, roughly \
exponential gradient from head to tail. The gene hunchback reads this \
gradient and switches from strongly on to off across a sharp boundary at \
mid-embryo. Fits of hunchback expression against Bicoid concentration give \
Hill coefficients of about 5, with reported values between about 4 and 10 \
depending on the method and the stage [0.6\[Dash]0.9].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e47e56ba-1c2a-456b-9111-1ab4f7b1c0e4"],

Cell["\<\
Photo 0.3. The fruit fly Drosophila melanogaster, about 2.5 mm long. Andr\
\[EAcute] Karwath (Aka), CC BY-SA 2.5, Wikimedia Commons.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontSize->14,
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->"6e42fdfe-2b7e-40b1-9727-53f993113370"],

