Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0.5 Population growth", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3e241494-1be9-48d9-a2cc-c8929135728f"],

Cell["\<\
A population with plenty of food grows exponentially, then slows as resources \
run short, and levels off at the carrying capacity K. Verhulst introduced a \
model for this in 1838 and in 1845 named its solution the logistic curve \
[0.12]. G. F. Gause's Paramecium experiments of the 1930s are the classic \
test: each species grown alone showed logistic growth to a stable carrying \
capacity [0.13].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"354480b2-5421-4579-812d-bbec6623bac6"],

Cell["\<\
Photo 0.5. Paramecium aurelia under the optical microscope, the species of \
Figure 0.5. Barfooz, CC BY-SA 3.0, Wikimedia Commons.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontSize->14,
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->"8e3acb4c-2c61-4072-9ded-b634a3e5e729"],

